From e31fa8b050dd312dbdbb2678028bad517c3d8c25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stepkun <stephan.kunz@kabelbw.de>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:40:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] software: only blend paths inside the dirty region

With partial rendering (RepaintBufferType::ReusedBuffer), paths were
blended with their coverage mask over the whole clip, also outside of the
redrawn region where the buffer is not cleared. Their anti-aliased edges
built up with every frame.

Paths are now blended only into the non-overlapping parts of the dirty
region inside the clip, like the other primitives of RenderToBuffer.

The screenshot tests now also check partial rendering into a buffer, as
they already did for line-by-line rendering (which doesn't draw paths).

ChangeLog: software: Fixed paths drawn wrongly with partial rendering into a buffer

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
